Dialogue: 2,0:00:00.00,0:00:07.34,Cue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Build a simple side table with Rectangle,\NPush/Pull, Make Object, Move, and Move Copy.
Dialogue: 2,0:00:07.34,0:00:15.04,Cue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Choose Rectangle. Pick opposite corners to draw\Na tabletop sixty centimeters wide and deep.
Dialogue: 2,0:00:15.04,0:00:22.89,Cue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Choose Push/Pull, select the face, and pull it\Nupward. Type three for the tabletop thickness.
Dialogue: 2,0:00:22.89,0:00:30.51,Cue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Select the tabletop geometry and choose Make\NObject. This keeps it separate from the legs.
Dialogue: 2,0:00:30.51,0:00:38.36,Cue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}With Move, lift the tabletop forty-two centimeters.\NIts upper surface is now forty-five high.
Dialogue: 2,0:00:38.36,0:00:46.91,Cue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Draw a four-centimeter square below a corner. Pull\Nit up forty-two centimeters, then make it an object.
Dialogue: 2,0:00:46.91,0:00:54.54,Cue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}Use Move Copy to make a second leg. Select\Nboth legs and copy them across to the far side.
Dialogue: 2,0:00:54.54,0:01:02.89,Cue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,120)}The table is complete: one top and four linked legs.\NSave the project, then explore your own design.
